'' A 'byval'-MARKED ARGUMENT AGAINST A BYREF PARAMETER WAS NOT VIABLE, so the call came
'' out UNTYPED and every use of its result declined. The value stands in for the
'' ADDRESS, which is the whole point of the spelling; costing it against the
'' parameter's own type asked the wrong question. Measured -- fbc writes
'' 'FZ( (char*)0ll )' and nothing else. udt-zstring/zwstring-params.bas is six of them.
''
'' A POINTER OR A POINTER-WIDE INTEGER and nothing else: a float has no address to
'' stand for and a string is a descriptor, so neither is viable.
''
'' Lowering had two matching holes. The string paths claimed the argument and had no
'' answer for the literal 0, so a 'byref as zstring' parameter declined even once the
'' call was typed -- a byval-marked argument now goes straight out as the pointer. And
'' ParamIsByref indexed the N_PROC's children by parameter NUMBER, but an N_PROC's
'' children are not all N_PARAM: ParamTypeAt and ParamIsArray beside it both walk, and
'' this one did not.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: --dump-ir tests/mir/src/byval-to-byref.bas
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-OUT: verify: ok
'' EXPECT-OUT: 0 statements not lowered
'' GOLDEN: expected/byval-to-byref.out
